  "config.yaml": "# yaml-language-server: $schema=./config.schema.json\n#\n# What work Chernabog does in this repo, and how. Committed, so the whole team\n# shares it. Each person's machine config (~/.config/chernabog/config.yaml)\n# decides which flows run for them, when, and with which agent.\n\nbaseBranch: main\n\n# Run in a fresh worktree before the agent starts. null for none.\ninstall: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\n\n# Commands the change must pass before its pull request opens.\nlocalGate: []\n\n# Decisions the agent must stop for and leave to a person.\nhumanOnly: []\n\n# Paths a change must not touch; one that does goes to a person instead of a pull request.\nhumanOnlyPaths:\n  - .github/**\n\n# Repo facts the agent should know.\nnotes: []\n\n# Default schedule for every flow, as cron. Unset spreads repos across the hour.\n# schedule: \"17 * * * *\"\n\n# Who runs the flows, by GitHub login. Unset: anyone. A default, not a gate:\n# chernabog enroll offers the flows ticked only to these logins, and anyone can\n# still pick them.\n# runners: [alice]\n\n# The reviewer pool, by GitHub login. A pull request with green CI asks one\n# of them at random to review it, never its author; review runs as that\n# persona, and re-review when it's asked again. On the automated path (an\n# auto:ship pull request) the approving reviewer merges, so each needs write\n# access to the repo. Unset: the pull request is labelled for a person to review.\n# reviewers: [alice, bob]\n\n# Per flow: schedule, concurrency, enabled (the default chernabog enroll\n# offers), agent, runners, assignee and reviewRequested. A reviewer on another agent than the one that wrote the code\n# avoids a model approving its own work; it runs under that agent's account in\n# machine config. assignee and reviewRequested work like GitHub's assignee: and\n# review-requested: qualifiers: \"@me\" (this machine's GitHub login), a login,\n# none, or a list. A machine starts only the work they match.\n# flows:\n#   implement:\n#     assignee: [\"@me\", none]\n#   review:\n#     agent: codex\n#     reviewRequested: \"@me\"\n\n# Where interactive agent sessions run: orca, tmux, headless (claude -p) or a\n# launcher a person defines in their machine config. Each person can choose\n# their own in machine config; launcher here is only the default,\n# and allowedLaunchers limits what they may choose. Unset: any launcher, with\n# headless as the default.\n# launcher: orca\n# allowedLaunchers: [orca, tmux, headless]\n\nlimits:\n  localGateRounds: 2\n  ciRounds: 3\n  # Re-reviews of one pull request before a person takes over.\n  reviewRounds: 1\n  staleAfter: 6 hours\n  ciTimeout: 2 hours\n  # The least time between two ticks events ask for, for one persona's flow.\n  # eventTickMin: 30 seconds\n  # Tasks one plan may hold, and the plan recipe's attempts to fix one that fails its checks.\n  planNodes: 12\n  planRounds: 2\n",
  "stages/README.md": "# Steps\n\nA flow runs a step from this directory with `step(\"name\", input)`. Each runs in its own process.\n\n- **Effect step:** `name.ts`, exporting `defineStage({ name, input, output, run })` from `@chernabog/sdk` as its default. It gets the SDK's services and types.\n- **Shell step:** an executable `name`. It reads `{ input, repo, run }` as JSON on stdin and prints its output as JSON on the last line of stdout.\n\nEither way: exit 0 to continue, 78 to skip the run, anything else to fail it. A step that crashes partway runs again, so it must be safe to repeat.\n",
